.TH WLCROSSHAIR 1 "2026-08-24" "wlcrosshair 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlcrosshair \- crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlcrosshair
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlcrosshair
is a minimal crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors that support the
wlr-layer-shell protocol (e.g.\& Hyprland, Sway, COSMIC, KDE Plasma).
.PP
It runs as a background daemon, drawing a crosshair image on a layer-shell
surface at the overlay layer, above all other windows including fullscreen
applications and games.  It listens on a Unix socket for commands from
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1).
.PP
The crosshair starts hidden.  Use
.B wlcrosshairctl
to toggle, show, hide, or reload the overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
(respects
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.SS Config Fields
.TP
.BI path " = " PATH
.I (required)
Path to a PNG crosshair image.  Tilde expansion is supported.
.TP
.BI output " = " NAME
.I (required)
Wayland output name as reported by the compositor (e.g.\&
.BR DP-1 ,
.BR eDP-1 ,
.BR HDMI-A-1 ).
See
.B FINDING THE OUTPUT NAME
below.
.TP
.BI size " = " PIXELS
.I (required if width/height not set)
Set both width and height to this value.
.TP
.BI width " = " PIXELS
.I (required if size not set)
Width of the crosshair in pixels.
.TP
.BI height " = " PIXELS
.I (required if size not set)
Height of the crosshair in pixels.
.TP
.BI opacity " = " VALUE
.I (optional; defaults to 1.0)
Opacity multiplier from 0.0 (invisible) to 1.0 (original image opacity).
The value multiplies the PNG image's existing alpha, so transparent pixels
remain transparent.
.SS Example Config
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
path = "~/.config/wlcrosshair/crosshair.png"
output = "DP-1"
size = 24
opacity = 0.75
.fi
.RE
.SH FINDING THE OUTPUT NAME
Run the command for your compositor inside its Wayland session and copy the
name of the display where the crosshair should appear:
.TP
.B KDE Plasma: kscreen-doctor -o
In "Output: 1 eDP-1 ...", use "eDP-1", not the numeric ID "1".
.TP
.B Hyprland: hyprctl monitors
In "Monitor eDP-1 (ID 0):", use "eDP-1", not "0" or the description.
.TP
.B Sway: swaymsg -t get_outputs
Use the output's "name" value, not its make or model.
.TP
.B COSMIC: cosmic-randr list
Use the name at the start of an entry, e.g.\& "eDP-1 (enabled)".
.TP
.B Other wlroots-based compositors (river, Wayfire, labwc): wlr-randr
Use the name before the quoted description, e.g.\& "DP-1".
This requires wlr-output-management support.
.TP
.B niri: niri msg outputs
Use the connector name in parentheses (e.g.\& "DP-1"), not the quoted
monitor description.
.PP
For other Wayland compositors, consult their output listing command.
.B wayland-info
may show an output name if the compositor advertises
.BR zxdg_output_manager_v1 ;
do not use a numeric ID, monitor description or model instead.  The
.B wlr-randr
command is not generally available on KWin or COSMIC.  A compositor must
provide a usable output name via
.B zxdg_output_manager_v1
and support
.B zwlr_layer_shell_v1
for this program to work; GNOME does not provide the required layer-shell
protocol.
.PP
Set the discovered name in
.IR ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml ,
for example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
output = "eDP-1"
.fi
.RE
Check it again after changing ports or docks.
.SH SOCKET
.B wlcrosshair
listens on
.I /tmp/crosshair.sock
for IPC commands (one per line).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the config directory.  Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1)
